{"name":"Delicate Truffle","hex":"#aa9c8b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"delicate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily damaged or requiring careful handling.","Characterized by a fine structure or thin lines."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A delicate item of clothing, especially underwear or lingerie.","A choice dainty; a delicacy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicate"},{"term":"truffle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various edible fungi, of the genus Tuber, that grow in the soil in southern Europe; the earthnut.","Ellipsis of chocolate truffle (“creamy chocolate confection, in the form of a ball, covered with cocoa powder”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/1280px-White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/